{"aggregate_id": "01M574ET5QJEBJC6N9RD7BYVJA", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M574ETC44FFBSQ68QC1ZEYJJ", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn.dejongh@sddevelopment.be", "created_at": "2026-10-18T09:11:05.158323+00:00", "friendly_name": "Mission-lifecycle event reconciliation", "mission_id": "01M574ET5QJEBJC6N9RD7BYVJA", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "mission-lifecycle-reconciliation-01M574ET", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Scope item B of 4.x rework epic #117. Brownfield grounding found the mission-lifecycle contracts are largely aligned with core already; the real gaps are additive and narrow: MissionReopened and FollowUpRecorded are modelled in Python but have no JSON schema or conformance fixtures, and ReviewerSelfApproval is emitted by core as a lifecycle event but modelled only in the producer_contract subsystem, not the project_lifecycle layer. This mission mirrors core's current shapes INTO the package (never importing core), additively and fail-closed, so every mission-lifecycle event core produces has a committed schema and fixture. Populating LOCAL_ONLY_EVENT_TYPES is excluded (owned by Mission A #118); mirroring SignificanceEvaluated/DecisionTimeoutExpired is deferred pending an operator decision on a RACI actor-shape change.", "purpose_tldr": "Close the schema+fixture gaps so the mission-lifecycle event contracts this package ships match what core currently emits and consumes.", "target_branch": "issue-119-mission-lifecycle-reconciliation", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty-events", "project_uuid": "bebf8d60-7c5d-4459-94b6-e0f3e4ad83f9", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-18T09:11:05.348787+00:00"}
